{"uncertainty": 0.15, "outcome": "rtl_bug", "artifacts": [{"kind": "root_cause_analysis", "title": "Root cause: uart_tx reloads its data holding register on a start pulse while busy", "summary": "Requirement [requirement:req-d10c4df532]. Failure as reported: the triage repro fails 1 of 4 checks and reaches $finish at 546000 [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e2] [run:run-0002]. VeriTriage gave unknown_failure at 30% confidence with top hypothesis 'Likely RTL bug' [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e1] [run:run-0001]. Because that confidence is low, it was treated as one candidate only. Defect location: in [artifact:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.a1], a statement 'if (start) hold <= data;' sits before the state case. It therefore runs in every state, including START, DATA and STOP. This contradicts the file's own header: 'A start pulse while a frame is in flight is ignored.' The IDLE branch already loads hold, so the outer load is redundant when idle and wrong when busy. Causality: a start pulse during DATA overwrites hold. The DATA state then drives tx <= hold[bit_idx+1] from the new byte, so the bits after the pulse come from the wrong data. The serialized byte becomes a mix of the old and new bytes, and the byte-compare check fails. Incorrectness: the specified behaviour is to ignore start while busy, and hold must stay constant for the whole frame. The fix direction is to remove the unconditional load and keep the load inside IDLE only. Hypotheses ranked: (1) rtl_bug: supported by reading the code against the header clause. It would be refuted if the new repro passed on this RTL. (2) testbench_bug: the new repro derives every expected value from the header (8N1, LSB first, start ignored while busy), not from RTL output. It is designed to pass on RTL without the outer load. It would be refuted only if the clean RTL also failed this repro. (3) infrastructure: the triage reproduction was deterministic and reached $finish [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e2], which argues against a tool or build cause. It would be supported if a clean rebuild changed the result. (4) spec_ambiguity: rejected because the header clause explicitly fixes the behaviour for a start pulse in flight."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/uart_tx_reload_repro_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking repro: start pulse during a frame must not corrupt it", "summary": "Repro for [artifact:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.a1], serving [requirement:req-d10c4df532]. The testbench sends 0xA5 and pulses start with 0x3C during data bit 2. It then checks five things: idle after reset, the start bit, the received byte equals 0xA5, the stop bit, and idle with no extra frame afterwards. Expected values come from the 8N1 header clause. Intended result: the byte check fails on the approved RTL (it receives 0x3D) and all checks pass on RTL that ignores start while busy. It prints a single NIRMAAN-SIM verdict with the run nonce before $finish, and includes a watchdog.", "entry": "uart_tx_reload_repro_tb"}], "tool_runs": ["run-0001", "run-0002"], "claims": ["The new repro testbench has not been simulated by me; whether it fails on the approved RTL is for the platform's simulator.run (expect=fail) gate to establish.", "Hand analysis predicts the approved RTL serializes 0x3D instead of 0xA5 in this repro (bits 0-2 from 0xA5, bits 3-7 from 0x3C).", "Hand analysis predicts the same testbench passes on RTL with the unconditional 'if (start) hold <= data;' removed.", "Independent review of this root-cause analysis is still required and has not been obtained."], "escalation": null, "notes": "The triage testbench content and the regression log were not provided to me, so I cannot confirm which check failed in run-0002. My conclusion rests on reading the RTL against its header specification. The proposed fix, removing the outer hold load, is not applied here; it belongs to a downstream task."}

=== FILE: tb/uart_tx_reload_repro_tb.v ===
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
// Repro: per the uart_tx specification (8N1, LSB first, "a start pulse while a
// frame is in flight is ignored"), a start pulse during the data bits must not
// change the byte being transmitted. Expected values come from the spec only.
module uart_tx_reload_repro_tb;
    localparam integer CPB = 4;
    localparam [7:0] BYTE_A = 8'hA5;  // frame actually started
    localparam [7:0] BYTE_B = 8'h3C;  // offered while busy; must be ignored

    reg        clk   = 1'b0;
    reg        rst   = 1'b1;
    reg        start = 1'b0;
    reg  [7:0] data  = 8'h00;
    wire       tx;
    wire       busy;

    uart_tx #(.CLKS_PER_BIT(CPB)) dut (
        .clk(clk), .rst(rst), .start(start), .data(data), .tx(tx), .busy(busy)
    );

    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    integer passed = 0;
    integer failed = 0;
    integer i;
    reg [7:0] rx;
    reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;
    reg finished = 1'b0;

    task check(input cond, input [8*48-1:0] what);
        begin
            if (cond) passed = passed + 1;
            else begin
                failed = failed + 1;
                $display("FAIL: %0s", what);
            end
        end
    endtask

    task finish_run;
        begin
            if (!finished) begin
                finished = 1'b1;
                $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
                $finish;
            end
        end
    endtask

    initial begin
        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce))
            nonce = "unset";
        repeat (3) @(negedge clk);
        rst = 1'b0;
        @(negedge clk);
        check(tx === 1'b1 && busy === 1'b0, "line idle after reset");

        fork
            begin : stimulus
                @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b1; data = BYTE_A;
                @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b0; data = 8'h00;
                // land in the middle of data bit 2
                repeat (14) @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b1; data = BYTE_B;
                @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b0; data = 8'h00;
            end
            begin : monitor
                @(negedge tx);
                repeat (CPB/2) @(negedge clk);
                check(tx === 1'b0 && busy === 1'b1, "start bit low, busy high");
                for (i = 0; i < 8; i = i + 1) begin
                    repeat (CPB) @(negedge clk);
                    rx[i] = tx;
                end
                if (rx !== BYTE_A)
                    $display("received 0x%02h, expected 0x%02h", rx, BYTE_A);
                check(rx === BYTE_A, "byte unchanged by start while busy");
                repeat (CPB) @(negedge clk);
                check(tx === 1'b1, "stop bit high");
            end
        join

        repeat (4*CPB) @(negedge clk);
        check(tx === 1'b1 && busy === 1'b0, "idle after frame, no second frame");
        finish_run;
    end

    initial begin
        #20000;
        $display("FAIL: watchdog timeout");
        failed = failed + 1;
        finish_run;
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===
